msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:60 26da42b565694385a2b00219a97b2a13
msgid ""
"`src/findfmt/models.py` defines core data structures (`FileInfo`, "
"`TraversalStats`) using `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)` for high "
"performance and reduced memory footprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:62 b5543f6c878343559f588ccf23188115
msgid ""
"The `slots` argument was introduced in Python 3.10. On Python 3.9 and "
"earlier, invoking `@dataclass(slots=True)` raises `TypeError: dataclass()"
" got an unexpected keyword argument 'slots'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:66 2249da9d0418410cb59feb3308728c64
msgid "**PEP 604 Union Syntax (`str | None`, `Path | str`)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:68 6d9d16cf2667404d8b136013963eeb58
msgid ""
"While `from __future__ import annotations` postpones evaluation of type "
"annotations in standard code on Python 3.7+, frameworks like Typer and "
"Click inspect type annotations at runtime to construct CLI options and "
"type coercion logic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:71 411780d7bff044f39340b57bd621ca42
msgid ""
"Evaluating union syntax (`str | None`) at runtime in Python 3.9 and "
"earlier triggers `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: 'type' "
"and 'type'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:74 34ca84b2ed9d446fb22d77dd522b9aca
msgid "**Standard Library Configuration Parsing**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:76 6cd1994700154a86ad3e2906f9879918
msgid ""
"Python 3.11+ includes `tomllib` (PEP 680) in the standard library, so "
"`findfmt` imports it directly. The `tomli` shim that Python 3.10 required"
" has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:79 fd5702df3e0144f38912f8ffdf2b4f61
msgid "**`typing.Self` (PEP 673)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:81 c56ac78c8793424484a67b45ae378741
msgid ""
"Python 3.11+ provides `typing.Self`, which `findfmt` uses for context-"
"manager return types. The `typing_extensions.Self` fallback that Python "
"3.10 required has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:83 89a5b02fda8942918ee4f8e5d3aaea55
msgid ""
"`typing.override` (PEP 698) only arrived in Python 3.12, so `typing-"
"extensions` remains a dependency on Python 3.11."
msgstr ""

