#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:94 df1aec98e8b54a99a98e13aa21bf338c
msgid "2.4. Maintenance Cost vs. Upstream EOL Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:96 a67af78ec7cb404582e57d3fcf82bb12
msgid "Python 3.6 reached End-of-Life (EOL) in December 2021."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:97 d4b0f7e025864b78880228036e21162c
msgid "Python 3.7 reached EOL in June 2023."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:98 bf35ed88818546ed99a72144a40e4abb
msgid "Python 3.8 reached EOL in October 2024."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:99 678b5ba81ebb4deab4aac6a7a5d2b44f
msgid "Python 3.9 reached EOL in October 2025."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:100 caac09dcec154db4971ce1298af5a246
msgid "Python 3.10 reached EOL on October 1, 2026."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:101 72e7efae863249519ad15c8b8dcfc140
msgid ""
"Python 3.11 is the oldest currently maintained Python version receiving "
"security updates (through October 2027)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/compatibility.md:104 29e049726ca34174a6ce1d6a90396c86
msgid ""
"Supporting Python < 3.10 would require downgrading data models, "
"discarding `slots=True`, introducing verbose `typing.Union` constructs, "
"and freezing dependencies to outdated versions with unpatched "
"vulnerabilities. Python 3.10 itself no longer receives security fixes, "
"and dependencies have started shipping security fixes only for Python "
"3.11+ (for example, `filelock` 4.2.1). Supporting it would also keep the "
"`tomli` and `typing_extensions.Self` shims alive. Therefore, `requires-"
"python = \">=3.11\"` is technically sound and necessary."
msgstr ""

